He left.

00:03:31.320 --> 00:03:33.050
Oh my, he forgot this.

00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:45.860
Saigou-kun, huh?

00:03:51.790 --> 00:03:53.860
Koushi-dono, you look fantastic today!

00:03:53.890 --> 00:03:55.150
Uh... Excuse me.

00:03:57.130 --> 00:03:58.630
I'm looking for someone.

00:03:59.170 --> 00:04:01.840
Do you know a guy named Saigou Katsuyuki?

00:04:02.680 --> 00:04:05.230
I think he's a student of this school.

00:04:06.200 --> 00:04:07.580
Saigou-dono?

00:04:07.870 --> 00:04:09.280
Saigou Katsuyuki...

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:11.760
I think I've heard of it somewhere...

00:04:11.980 --> 00:04:14.400
Saigou Katsuyuki... Saigou Katsuyuki...

00:04:14.550 --> 00:04:14.990
Saigou...

00:04:15.090 --> 00:04:16.310
Saigou!?

00:04:18.670 --> 00:04:20.740
Is that the Saigou you are looking for...?

00:04:21.460 --> 00:04:22.750
Yeah, that's him.

00:04:23.370 --> 00:04:24.030
Thank you.

00:04:30.970 --> 00:04:32.390
Do you remember me?

00:04:34.020 --> 00:04:34.610
Come on...

00:04:34.770 --> 00:04:37.060
Last night, at the parking lot under the overpass...

00:04:37.820 --> 00:04:45.480
Note: The first part sounded like "you almost assaulted me" in Japanese.

00:04:37.820 --> 00:04:40.390
That's right, the person who was almost assaulted...

00:04:43.500 --> 00:04:45.480
...and you saved me.

00:04:47.550 --> 00:04:49.240
Here, your jacket.

00:04:51.250 --> 00:04:53.580
The person I owe my life to forgot this.

00:04:54.050 --> 00:04:55.810
So I thought I have to take it back no matter what.

00:04:58.350 --> 00:04:59.790
Huh? What's wrong?

00:05:01.430 --> 00:05:05.410
He wants to know how you found this school.

00:05:07.300 --> 00:05:09.310
Your bus pass was in the jacket.

00:05:09.650 --> 00:05:10.940
Your name was on it too.

00:05:12.070 --> 00:05:14.420
"Oh, I see. I'm convinced." He says.

00:05:15.930 --> 00:05:17.970
Hey, we should go to our class.

00:05:18.880 --> 00:05:20.890
Thanks for showing me the way.

00:05:21.080 --> 00:05:22.080
I'm leaving.

00:05:24.380 --> 00:05:25.850
Wait, what's your name?

00:05:27.420 --> 00:05:28.900
I'm Alice.

00:05:29.020 --> 00:05:30.400
I'm a street musician.

00:05:30.810 --> 00:05:34.450
I'm playing in the central park these days, come and listen if you have time.

00:05:35.960 --> 00:05:38.790
Thank you for the jacket!

00:05:40.330 --> 00:05:43.180
How can you understand him?

00:05:45.160 --> 00:05:48.990
People in love are connected by heart.

00:05:49.460 --> 00:05:49.960
Huh?

00:05:50.750 --> 00:05:54.270
It looks like Saigou-dono likes Alice-dono.

00:05:54.490 --> 00:05:55.400
Really?

00:05:57.880 --> 00:05:59.790
What do you want for dinner?

00:06:00.360 --> 00:06:00.980
Something good.

00:06:01.640 --> 00:06:05.290
Then let's have your favorite, sablefish.

00:06:05.510 --> 00:06:05.980
Huh?

00:06:07.330 --> 00:06:07.890
What is it?

00:06:08.240 --> 00:06:09.180
Over there...

00:06:09.490 --> 00:06:09.710
Huh?

00:06:15.930 --> 00:06:17.310
Welcome.

00:06:17.660 --> 00:06:18.030
Mmm?

00:06:19.040 --> 00:06:20.420
Excuse me...

00:06:20.890 --> 00:06:22.330
How may I help you...?

00:06:24.280 --> 00:06:26.760
He wants 50 roses.

00:06:28.580 --> 00:06:30.560
50... roses?

00:06:31.030 --> 00:06:32.380
Please.

00:06:33.200 --> 00:06:34.580
Yes, right away!

00:06:35.080 --> 00:06:35.650
Roses...

00:06:35.770 --> 00:06:37.620
Are they for Alice-dono?

00:06:43.210 --> 00:06:44.000
Are you serious?

00:06:44.750 --> 00:06:51.000
Good bye. When we meet again,

00:06:44.750 --> 00:06:51.000
サヨナラ また会う時に君は

00:06:44.750 --> 00:06:51.000
sayonara mata au toki ni kimi wa

00:06:51.270 --> 00:06:57.400
I wonder if your dream will be fulfilled.

00:06:51.270 --> 00:06:57.400
描いてた夢をかなえてるかな

00:06:51.270 --> 00:06:57.400
egaiteta yume wo kanaeteru kana

00:06:57.750 --> 00:07:03.960
Walking away from me, I silently look at your back.

00:06:57.750 --> 00:07:03.960
歩き出す君の背中にそっと

00:06:57.750 --> 00:07:03.960
aruki dasu kimi no senaka ni sotto

00:07:04.280 --> 00:07:06.920
I want to tell you,

00:07:04.280 --> 00:07:06.920
送りたいよ

00:07:04.280 --> 00:07:06.920
okuritai yo

00:07:07.100 --> 00:07:09.490
good luck.

00:07:07.100 --> 00:07:09.490
頑張って

00:07:07.100 --> 00:07:09.490
ganbatte

00:07:17.430 --> 00:07:20.070
Saigou-kun, you've come.

00:07:21.830 --> 00:07:23.210
What are those roses for?

00:07:27.570 --> 00:07:28.360
For me?

00:07:29.330 --> 00:07:30.310
Thank you!

00:07:32.100 --> 00:07:32.910
They are so pretty.

00:07:34.040 --> 00:07:35.050
Nice fragrant.

00:07:39.690 --> 00:07:41.670
It's the first time since I've come to this town...

00:07:43.400 --> 00:07:45.850
...that I received applause and flowers.

00:07:46.790 --> 00:07:50.340
You are my number one fan in this town.

00:07:51.970 --> 00:07:53.570
You are not glad...

00:07:53.880 --> 00:07:55.480
...for being the number one fan?

00:08:00.450 --> 00:08:00.980
Oh, yeah.

00:08:01.800 --> 00:08:05.810
I'm still not sure what to name the song I just played.

00:08:06.250 --> 00:08:08.480
Do you have any good idea, Saigou-kun?

00:08:11.530 --> 00:08:15.610
It's a song of departure, so I want to use words you would say at that time.

00:08:16.430 --> 00:08:18.400
I can't think of anything good.

00:08:20.190 --> 00:08:25.150
I've went to a lot of towns, and have experienced all kinds of departures.

00:08:26.060 --> 00:08:29.420
But I was never able to turn them into words.

00:08:31.340 --> 00:08:33.850
Do you know any good words?

00:08:39.340 --> 00:08:40.880
Stop, stop!

00:08:41.200 --> 00:08:43.270
You are going to explode.

00:08:45.750 --> 00:08:48.480
I don't want to lose my new fan.

00:08:55.230 --> 00:08:55.670
There.

00:08:56.050 --> 00:08:58.090
Commemoration sign for my number one fan.

00:08:59.410 --> 00:09:02.260
It's gonna worth a fortune in a few years, so take good care of it!

00:09:03.930 --> 00:09:05.500
Are you doubting me?

00:09:08.950 --> 00:09:09.960
I...

00:09:11.210 --> 00:09:14.290
...will perform on a big stage one of these days.

00:09:16.170 --> 00:09:17.870
One of these days... I'm sure.

00:09:25.280 --> 00:09:27.100
Which reference book should I get?

00:09:27.630 --> 00:09:29.360
If you wanna study economics and politics...

00:09:31.370 --> 00:09:32.500
Featured articles on dates...

00:09:32.840 --> 00:09:36.420
Now to think of it, I haven't went out with Koushi-dono for a while...

00:09:40.940 --> 00:09:42.200
Thank you very much.

00:09:43.140 --> 00:09:44.180
Inuzuka-kun.

00:09:44.430 --> 00:09:46.880
Thank you for helping me choosing the reference book.

00:09:47.290 --> 00:09:50.930
Talk to me anytime if you need any help on study.

00:09:51.120 --> 00:09:54.380
Koushi-dono, I need help too.

00:09:54.510 --> 00:09:55.450
What is it?

00:09:57.460 --> 00:10:02.040
Please lend your knowledge for Saigou-dono's love!

00:10:02.860 --> 00:10:04.020
Then the first round...

00:10:04.650 --> 00:10:08.920
Let's start the "this is the perfect date" brainstorm session!

00:10:10.300 --> 00:10:10.770
Hey.

00:10:11.050 --> 00:10:12.650
Why are you guys here?

00:10:13.030 --> 00:10:14.950
Come on, don't mind the petty details.

00:10:14.950 --> 00:10:18.710
I called them over because I think we can come up with better ideas with more people.

00:10:18.710 --> 00:10:19.280
Yeah, yeah.

00:10:19.310 --> 00:10:20.060
Me, me!

00:10:20.380 --> 00:10:22.290
How does window shopping sound?

00:10:22.540 --> 00:10:24.870
That's my sis, nice idea.

00:10:24.930 --> 00:10:27.720
It's especially great when your wallet is growing thin.

00:10:28.190 --> 00:10:30.670
I also recommend the department stores.

00:10:30.740 --> 00:10:31.650
That's right, that's right.

00:10:31.680 --> 00:10:34.030
You can eat food samples when you are hungry...

00:10:35.260 --> 00:10:37.580
Don't mention those disgraceful things in front of Koushi senpai.

00:10:38.680 --> 00:10:42.200
Where do you think is a good place for a date, class rep?

00:10:43.080 --> 00:10:44.390
How about the library?

00:10:44.550 --> 00:10:45.810
Rejected, rejected.

00:10:47.130 --> 00:10:50.270
Why don't you just go to the zoo or the amusement park?

00:10:50.740 --> 00:10:51.990
That's right.

00:10:52.310 --> 00:10:55.630
We went to the zoo last time, let's go to the amusement park this time!

00:10:55.730 --> 00:10:58.080
Hey, I'm not talking about us!

00:11:00.090 --> 00:11:02.130
I'm sorry, I'll think harder.

00:11:04.080 --> 00:11:05.900
He thinks the amusement park is a good idea.

00:11:06.530 --> 00:11:08.100
Uh... Koushi-dono...

00:11:08.220 --> 00:11:08.820
Huh?

00:11:09.040 --> 00:11:13.940
How about let's have a double date together?

00:11:14.470 --> 00:11:16.610
We are gonna be a bother if we tag along.

00:11:18.490 --> 00:11:22.380
"That's reassuring, I like it." He says!

00:11:24.140 --> 00:11:25.770
Just do whatever you want...

00:11:30.420 --> 00:11:34.060
<i>"Would you like to go to the amusement park next Sunday with us?"</i>

00:11:34.500 --> 00:11:35.350
<i>He says!</i>

00:11:36.890 --> 00:11:37.960
Amusement park, huh?

00:11:38.110 --> 00:11:39.240
I'm so looking forward to it.

00:11:39.680 --> 00:11:46.720
You don't look like the best assassin from the Uzuki clan when you say that.

00:11:48.070 --> 00:11:50.950
I've been looking for you, Uzuki Alice-san.

00:11:53.650 --> 00:11:56.100
You guys are really persistent.

00:11:56.260 --> 00:12:00.250
The traitor must be punished no matter where she escapes to.

00:12:00.500 --> 00:12:02.510
That's the rule of our clan.

00:12:03.420 --> 00:12:06.490
I'll send you guys home no matter how many times you come.

00:12:06.870 --> 00:12:10.950
And then you'll hide yourself in another city.

00:12:12.020 --> 00:12:14.340
Aren't you growing tired of a life like that?

00:12:14.940 --> 00:12:20.180
Unable to find a friend who you can trust, departure shortly awaits the people who you've just met.

00:12:20.210 --> 00:12:21.630
That's none of your business.

00:12:23.230 --> 00:12:24.990
I just don't understand.

00:12:25.390 --> 00:12:30.230
With the influence of our clan, you can penetrate the show business easily, yet you decided to betray us.

00:12:30.890 --> 00:12:36.600
Moreover, living the life of a fugitive, how are you planning to become a musician?

00:12:37.360 --> 00:12:42.950
When you stand on the glittering stage, the guest seats will only be full of assassins who are after your life.

00:12:43.760 --> 00:12:45.460
That's none of your business.

00:12:48.000 --> 00:12:49.700
Let's make a deal.

00:12:50.610 --> 00:12:51.550
A deal?

00:12:52.050 --> 00:12:56.350
If you help us assassinate a person, I will grant you freedom.

00:12:58.390 --> 00:12:59.520
Thi... This is...

00:13:00.120 --> 00:13:02.410
Make Inuzuka Koushi disappear.

00:13:03.010 --> 00:13:04.990
It's a request from the Uzuki clan.

00:13:05.460 --> 00:13:09.000
And it looks like you know Inuzuka Koushi already.

00:13:09.070 --> 00:13:10.700
Piece of cake, isn't it?

00:13:11.610 --> 00:13:12.550
You bastard...

00:13:12.650 --> 00:13:13.740
Oh, by the way.

00:13:13.960 --> 00:13:18.300
If you refuse, your sunglasses friend may find himself in some unexpected trouble.

00:13:19.300 --> 00:13:21.440
Think carefully about this.

00:13:22.160 --> 00:13:25.300
Work for your clan one last time...

00:13:25.520 --> 00:13:29.470
...or keep on running for the rest of your life.

00:13:29.880 --> 00:13:31.330
The choice is yours.

00:13:43.730 --> 00:13:45.990
Koushi-dono, it's a Ferris wheel!

00:13:46.240 --> 00:13:47.620
Yep, it's a Ferris wheel.

00:13:48.120 --> 00:13:49.980
There is a merry-go-round!

00:13:50.570 --> 00:13:52.710
And there are go-carts over there!

00:13:52.710 --> 00:13:54.090
Yeah, go-carts.

00:13:54.210 --> 00:13:56.130
Go go, go go!

00:13:56.760 --> 00:13:58.230
Momoko senpai!

00:13:58.890 --> 00:13:59.800
Hi there.

00:13:59.830 --> 00:14:01.620
Why are you guys here?

00:14:01.750 --> 00:14:03.700
We are working part-time here.

00:14:03.760 --> 00:14:04.950
I see!

00:14:05.010 --> 00:14:07.930
Now only if class rep-dono is here, everyone would be gathered.

00:14:08.030 --> 00:14:10.600
I'm sure the four eyes is in the library by herself.

00:14:13.050 --> 00:14:15.940
I wonder if Inuzuka-kun is having fun.

00:14:16.600 --> 00:14:18.260
Which one should we ride?

00:14:18.360 --> 00:14:19.930
How about the coffee cups?

00:14:20.810 --> 00:14:21.620
How about it?

00:14:22.380 --> 00:14:23.790
I don't really care.

00:14:24.130 --> 00:14:25.170
It looks like fun.

00:14:25.330 --> 00:14:25.800
Let's ride.

00:14:27.150 --> 00:14:28.910
Four riders, coming up!

00:14:32.670 --> 00:14:36.060
If I assassinate Koushi-kun, I can be free.

00:14:36.970 --> 00:14:37.630
And...

00:14:39.110 --> 00:14:41.750
Saigou-kun won't have to go through any danger.

00:14:45.330 --> 00:14:48.340
Koushi-kun, I don't hold any grudge against you...

00:14:49.090 --> 00:14:51.130
But I'm sorry, you have die.

00:14:51.640 --> 00:14:52.230
Look.

00:14:52.890 --> 00:14:54.090
It's a parade.

00:14:56.690 --> 00:14:57.600
Here we go!

00:14:59.610 --> 00:15:01.020
Shit, I missed!

00:15:02.090 --> 00:15:04.040
Hey, don't spin it all of a sudden!

00:15:04.230 --> 00:15:06.240
I'm sorry, I couldn't help myself...

00:15:08.650 --> 00:15:10.250
What's that?

00:15:10.690 --> 00:15:15.280
I have to help heat things up between senpai and onii-chan.

00:15:15.650 --> 00:15:17.730
Here is a big service on speed.

00:15:20.770 --> 00:15:22.000
The speed has suddenly...

00:15:22.120 --> 00:15:23.630
I can't aim like this.

00:15:23.910 --> 00:15:25.070
We are done...

00:15:26.110 --> 00:15:27.680
I feel sick...

00:15:27.900 --> 00:15:29.370
Let's ride that next!

00:15:29.370 --> 00:15:30.720
Note: The sign says "Jet Coaster", and then it follows with warnings on who shouldn't ride this.

00:15:31.790 --> 00:15:33.420
I'll settle it this time for sure.

00:15:35.690 --> 00:15:38.200
If we are this close, there is no way I can fail.

00:15:38.890 --> 00:15:41.900
But how do I fool the others...

00:15:43.220 --> 00:15:44.190
Where is Koushi-kun?

00:15:44.480 --> 00:15:46.450
Koushi-dono said he'll pass this one.

00:15:46.640 --> 00:15:47.240
Eh?

00:15:51.380 --> 00:15:52.450
Then I'm getting off too...

00:15:56.660 --> 00:15:58.480
What should we ride next?

00:15:58.980 --> 00:16:01.240
Slow down a bit.

00:16:01.740 --> 00:16:03.820
There is nothing we can do if those two are in that condition.

00:16:04.730 --> 00:16:06.390
It's not going as planned at all.

00:16:07.210 --> 00:16:09.780
But in order to not put Saigou-kun in any danger...

00:16:13.960 --> 00:16:14.960
Thank you.

00:16:15.430 --> 00:16:17.440
I'm just a little tired from all the rides.

00:16:21.210 --> 00:16:25.820
The assassination of Koushi-kun can only be done when there is no one else around.

00:16:29.150 --> 00:16:32.890
<i>That key chain would look great on Alice-dono!</i>

00:16:36.560 --> 00:16:37.600
Saigou-kun...

00:16:38.010 --> 00:16:39.510
I have a favor to ask...

00:16:54.140 --> 00:16:56.310
You want me to help you choosing a stuffed animal?

00:16:56.470 --> 00:16:57.940
If it's anything I can do!

00:16:58.630 --> 00:17:01.140
You are choosing a present for Alice-dono, right?

00:17:02.780 --> 00:17:04.100
Thank you, Saigou-kun.

00:17:05.010 --> 00:17:06.760
Now we can be alone.

00:17:07.390 --> 00:17:08.810
A... Alice-san?

00:17:08.840 --> 00:17:09.530
Where are we going?

00:17:09.560 --> 00:17:10.630
A good place.

00:17:11.630 --> 00:17:13.950
I see couples everywhere.

00:17:14.050 --> 00:17:16.470
Sis, you have me.

00:17:16.500 --> 00:17:19.040
Enough with the sleep-talk, just shut up and pick trash.

00:17:20.260 --> 00:17:21.140
Onii-chan...?

00:17:22.180 --> 00:17:25.130
Huh? Momoko senpai is not with him.

00:17:25.410 --> 00:17:26.760
I wonder what happened.

00:17:28.140 --> 00:17:29.240
It bothers me...

00:17:31.190 --> 00:17:32.380
A good place...

00:17:32.380 --> 00:17:33.890
Translation: Under construction.

00:17:33.230 --> 00:17:33.920
Is this the place?

00:17:40.080 --> 00:17:41.650
Don't tell me you are...

00:17:42.050 --> 00:17:42.590
That's right.

00:17:43.400 --> 00:17:46.610
I'm an assassin who's looking to kill you.

00:17:52.040 --> 00:17:52.820
You saw that?

00:17:53.040 --> 00:17:55.050
That woman is a martial artist.

00:17:55.210 --> 00:17:57.030
Let Momoko senpai know right away.

00:18:05.980 --> 00:18:07.200
Who are you?

00:18:07.520 --> 00:18:11.690
Makura Kakkaku Kagen style
Uzuki Alice

00:18:08.300 --> 00:18:11.600
I'm Uzuki Alice of the Makura Kakkaku Kagen style.

00:18:12.040 --> 00:18:14.420
Due to some reason, I have to take Koushi-kun's life.

00:18:14.700 --> 00:18:15.680
Don't bullshit with me!

00:18:20.420 --> 00:18:22.050
Did she hide into the shadow?

00:18:22.210 --> 00:18:22.870
Over there!

00:18:26.980 --> 00:18:27.670
Shit.

00:18:27.800 --> 00:18:28.680
Iroha-chan, behind you!

00:18:33.320 --> 00:18:33.820
You are slow.

00:18:34.420 --> 00:18:35.080
Shit.

00:18:35.960 --> 00:18:36.810
Iroha-chan!

00:18:37.720 --> 00:18:39.380
Now you can't interfere with me anymore.

00:18:40.390 --> 00:18:43.150
I'm sorry, I didn't want to do this.

00:18:44.370 --> 00:18:45.100
I have no choice.

00:18:49.050 --> 00:18:51.630
At least... I'll do it painlessly.

00:18:52.030 --> 00:18:52.980
Sto... Stop...!

00:18:54.040 --> 00:18:54.990
Farewell.

00:19:01.080 --> 00:19:04.750
I won't forgive anyone who tries to hurt Koushi-dono!

00:19:04.940 --> 00:19:05.600
Momoko!

00:19:06.010 --> 00:19:07.580
Rest assured, Koushi-dono.

00:19:07.890 --> 00:19:10.460
Now that I'm here, everything is gonna be alright.

00:19:12.540 --> 00:19:18.250
I didn't want Saigou-kun to see me as an assassin.

00:19:18.940 --> 00:19:19.980
Untie me already!

00:19:20.100 --> 00:19:22.460
I'm doing it, now just stop moving!

00:19:22.930 --> 00:19:24.000
At the very least...

00:19:24.720 --> 00:19:25.910
I'm sorry, Momoko-chan.

00:19:27.010 --> 00:19:29.240
So you are not gonna do as I wish.

00:19:35.140 --> 00:19:37.340
They were all bounced off...

00:19:37.720 --> 00:19:38.440
It's useless.

00:19:38.690 --> 00:19:40.890
Your skills will not work on me.

00:19:41.770 --> 00:19:43.740
Are you saying that we are on different levels?

00:19:44.530 --> 00:19:45.340
In that case...

00:19:45.500 --> 00:19:47.130
I'll just have to accomplish my mission.

00:19:48.520 --> 00:19:49.170
Shit!

00:19:53.100 --> 00:19:54.170
Saigou-dono!

00:19:54.290 --> 00:19:55.110
Saigou...

00:19:58.000 --> 00:19:59.100
Wh... Why...?

00:19:59.940 --> 00:20:01.510
Why did you interfere?

00:20:01.670 --> 00:20:04.940
I thought Saigou-kun is my only ally...

00:20:06.380 --> 00:20:07.290
Aren't you?

00:20:10.590 --> 00:20:12.220
Then step out of the way.

00:20:12.280 --> 00:20:13.910
If I don't accomplish my mission...

00:20:14.350 --> 00:20:15.520
If I don't...

00:20:25.560 --> 00:20:28.700
"Your hands were created to make music."

00:20:29.610 --> 00:20:31.650
"You mustn't taint them with blood."

00:20:31.970 --> 00:20:32.910
He says.

00:20:47.980 --> 00:20:50.110
Worthless traitor.

00:20:50.430 --> 00:20:51.560
What are you doing?

00:20:53.350 --> 00:20:56.300
Are you the gangster who's making a fuss recently?

00:20:57.400 --> 00:20:58.910
Sis, what do we do?

00:20:59.780 --> 00:21:00.880
Get him.

00:21:00.950 --> 00:21:03.580
NO!!

00:21:05.560 --> 00:21:06.630
Today is the day, right?

00:21:06.820 --> 00:21:08.890
When Alice-san goes to France.

00:21:09.140 --> 00:21:10.400
It's amazing.

00:21:10.620 --> 00:21:14.260
She's gonna study music abroad.

00:21:14.630 --> 00:21:16.830
Aren't you going to send her off?

00:21:17.110 --> 00:21:19.250
Aren't you worried that Saigou is going alone?

00:21:22.200 --> 00:21:24.250
I'm sure it's gonna be alright.

00:21:28.860 --> 00:21:30.300
In that case, Saigou-kun.

00:21:30.490 --> 00:21:31.400
Stay well.

00:21:35.360 --> 00:21:36.520
I can't do it.

00:21:36.830 --> 00:21:39.590
What I should say at a time like this...

00:21:40.500 --> 00:21:42.230
I just can't find good words to express myself.

00:21:48.890 --> 00:21:49.730
Good bye.

00:21:51.740 --> 00:21:57.520
In my cold and shivering left hand,

00:21:51.740 --> 00:21:57.520
かじかんだ左手の中

00:21:51.740 --> 00:21:57.520
kajikanda hidarite no naka

00:21:57.580 --> 00:22:03.110
it's a small ring.

00:21:57.580 --> 00:22:03.110
お揃いの小さなリング

00:21:57.580 --> 00:22:03.110
osoroi no chiisana ringu

00:22:03.830 --> 00:22:09.670
For the two who are far apart,

00:22:03.830 --> 00:22:09.670
遠く離れていた二人を

00:22:03.830 --> 00:22:09.670
tooku hanareteita futari wo

00:22:10.080 --> 00:22:15.890
it's the treasure that bounds them together.

00:22:10.080 --> 00:22:15.890
繋いでいたたからもの

00:22:10.080 --> 00:22:15.890
tsunaideita takaramono

00:22:19.400 --> 00:22:25.340
In the letter that arrived in early winter,

00:22:19.400 --> 00:22:25.340
冬の初めに届いた手紙

00:22:19.400 --> 00:22:25.340
fuyu no hajime ni todoita tegami

00:22:25.650 --> 00:22:31.710
there was a ring and the last word.

00:22:25.650 --> 00:22:31.710
一つの指輪と最後の言葉

00:22:25.650 --> 00:22:31.710
hitotsu no yubiwa to saigou no kotoba

00:22:31.740 --> 00:22:37.990
Good bye. When we meet again,

00:22:31.740 --> 00:22:37.990
サヨナラ また会う時に君は

00:22:31.740 --> 00:22:37.990
sayonara mata au toki ni kimi wa

00:22:38.120 --> 00:22:44.250
I wonder if your dream will be fulfilled.

00:22:38.120 --> 00:22:44.250
描いてた夢をかなえてるかな

00:22:38.120 --> 00:22:44.250
egaiteta yume wo kanaeteru kana

00:22:44.340 --> 00:22:50.550
Walking away from me, I silently look at your back.

00:22:44.340 --> 00:22:50.550
歩き出す君の背中にそっと

00:22:44.340 --> 00:22:50.550
aruki dasu kimi no senaka ni sotto

00:22:50.590 --> 00:22:53.230
I want to tell you,

00:22:50.590 --> 00:22:53.230
送りたいよ

00:22:50.590 --> 00:22:53.230
okuritaiyo

00:22:53.360 --> 00:22:56.840
good luck.

00:22:53.360 --> 00:22:56.840
Good Luck

00:23:07.500 --> 00:23:08.400
Good luck.

00:23:11.680 --> 00:23:13.590
In the next episode of Sumomomo Momomo,

00:23:14.630 --> 00:23:17.670
it's the story about "the way to break the period of weariness".

00:23:17.800 --> 00:23:18.870
Good luck.
